criteria:
Inclusion criteria:
1. Older than 18 years;
2. Undergoing elective mitral valve repair or replacement surgery with planned cardiopulmonary bypass via midline sternotomy or minithoracotomy;
3. Preoperative evidence of left ventricular end-systolic diameter >40 mm and/or left ventricular end-diastolic diameter >60 mm and/or left ventricular ejection fraction<60%;
4. Signed informed consent.
Exclusion criteria:
1. Need for preoperative dialysis;
2. Patients with hypersensitivity to the active substance or to any of the excipients;
3. Patients with severe bradycardia (less than 50 beats per minute) sick sinus syndrome, severe atrioventricular nodal conductance disorders or 2nd -3rd degree atrioventricular block and without a pacemaker;
4. Patients with cardiogenic shock, severe hypotension (MAP<50 mmHg), decompensated heart failure or severe pulmonary hypertension (PAPs >70 mmHg);
5. Patients with non-treated phaeochromocytoma;
6. Patients with acute asthmatic attack;
7. Patients with severe, uncorrectable metabolic acidosis.
8. Participation in a clinical trial in which an investigational drug was administered within 30 days of screening or within the 5 half-lives of the study drug, whichever is longer.
9. Hepatic dysfunction (defined as Child-Pugh class C);
10. History of previous unusual response to beta-blockers;
11. Urgent or emergency surgery;
12. Patient already in need of mechanical circulatory support before surgery (except for IABP);
13. Pregnancy as documented by a pregnancy test performed in the last 72h before surgery
14. Refusal or inability to sign the informed consent.
15. Patients with preoperative evidence of hypernatremia (serum sodium concentration: > 160 mmol/L);
16. Patients with preoperative evidence of hyperchloremia (serum chloride concentration: >115 mmol/L);
